body:
Since I was looking for a completely local tool, I want to inform you, that your tool currently binds to 0.0.0.0 and thereby exposes its port on LAN.
Changing the default bind to 127.0.0.1 and adding a ENV Variable for configuration if users do want to bind to 0.0.0.0 should be trivial.

Here is my diff (as I feel this change does not warrant a pull request and I seemingly cannot write one to this repo anyway).

```
PS C:\Users\rgraf\bin\myrlin-workbook> git show 0823f5f
commit 0823f5fc83376585b15d03600da96533fc44e7b0 (HEAD -> main)
Author: Robert Graf <rgraf@ivugmbh.de>
Date:   Fri Feb 13 13:14:19 2026 +0100

    Bind server to 127.0.0.1 by default, configurable via CWM_HOST

    Previously the server bound to 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces), making it
    reachable on the LAN. Now defaults to localhost-only. Set CWM_HOST=0.0.0.0
    to restore the old behavior when LAN/tunnel access is needed.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/gui.js b/src/gui.js
index 3f89727..8b7c5d1 100644
--- a/src/gui.js
+++ b/src/gui.js
@@ -84,9 +84,10 @@ if (process.argv.includes('--demo')) {
 // ─── Start Server ──────────────────────────────────────────

 const port = parseInt(process.env.PORT, 10) || 3456;
-const server = startServer(port);
+const host = process.env.CWM_HOST || '127.0.0.1';
+const server = startServer(port, host);

-console.log(`CWM GUI running at http://localhost:${port}`);
+console.log(`CWM GUI running at http://${host}:${port}`);
 console.log('Press Ctrl+C to stop.');

 // Snapshot frontend files as "last known good" on successful start
diff --git a/src/web/server.js b/src/web/server.js
index 6b0186f..1a1fe03 100644
--- a/src/web/server.js
+++ b/src/web/server.js
@@ -3972,11 +3972,11 @@ app.get('/api/workspaces/:id/conflicts', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
 // Reference to PTY manager for cleanup on shutdown
 let _ptyManager = null;

-function startServer(port = 3456) {
+function startServer(port = 3456, host = '127.0.0.1') {
   // Wire store events to SSE before accepting connections
   attachStoreEvents();

-  const server = app.listen(port, () => {
+  const server = app.listen(port, host, () => {
     // Server is ready - caller handles the log message
   });
```
